brcmfmac: advertise DWDS repeater capability, report per-station DWDS state

Broadcom's firmware on this chip family (confirmed live on BCM43602,
netgear,r8000) implements Dynamic WDS (DWDS) - a per-station 4-address
framing negotiation between DWDS-capable Broadcom APs/repeaters that
lets a backhaul link carry real client MAC addresses end-to-end,
without the NAT/proxy-ARP hiding a plain 3-address STA link forces on
userspace repeater tools (relayd and friends). The driver has carried
the firmware's own status bits for this since day one
(BRCMF_STA_DWDS_CAP, BRCMF_STA_DWDS in fwil_types.h) but never read or
acted on them anywhere, and NL80211_IFTYPE_WDS is unconditionally
rejected (-EOPNOTSUPP) in all three of add_iface/change_iface/del_iface
with no per-chip branch at all.

Confirmed empirically before writing this (not assumed): a small
out-of-tree probe module (hwoffload-research/psta-probe/dwds_probe.c),
built against this exact SDK/kernel tree, set the "dwds" iovar via
brcmf_fil_iovar_data_set() DOWN/UP-bracketed on the STA interface and
read it back - accepted and durably retained (err=0), where the
classic "wds" iovar is rejected outright (err=-52). That confirms the
firmware genuinely implements this and the iovar name/semantics are
real, not guessed.

This patch does two small, narrowly-scoped things:

1. brcmf_cfg80211_start_ap(): advertise DWDS capability on an AP-role
   bsscfg by setting "dwds"=1 via brcmf_fil_bsscfg_int_set(), the same
   per-bsscfg helper already used for wpa_auth/wsec/mfp just above it.
   Non-fatal if firmware rejects it (logged, not gated) - AP bring-up
   must never depend on it. This is advertisement only: it does not
   force 4-address framing on anything. An ordinary 802.11 client
   (a phone, an IoT camera) has no concept of DWDS, never sets
   BRCMF_STA_DWDS_CAP, and is completely unaffected either way.

2. brcmf_cfg80211_get_station(): read BRCMF_STA_DWDS_CAP/BRCMF_STA_DWDS
   out of the sta_info_le flags word already being decoded here, and
   log via brcmf_dbg(CONN, ...) when either bit is set. There is no
   existing generic nl80211 station-info field for "this station has a
   DWDS/4-address link active" (checked: no NL80211_STA_FLAG_4ADDR_MODE
   or equivalent exists anywhere in this tree) - a real UAPI attribute
   for that is an upstream API discussion in its own right, not
   something to invent unilaterally in an out-of-tree patch. This is
   deliberately log-only for now: real, honest observability (dmesg
   will show a peer negotiating DWDS if it ever does) without
   overclaiming a UAPI surface that doesn't exist yet.

Explicitly NOT claimed by this patch: this does not make an ordinary
client (a Eufy camera, a phone) get 4-address/MAC-preserving treatment
through a repeated AP - DWDS is a Broadcom-to-Broadcom (or wl/dhd-
compatible) peer negotiation, not a client-facing feature. It is only
useful when the *other end* of a backhaul link (another Broadcom-family
AP or repeater) also speaks DWDS. No such peer was available to test
against in this environment, so the negotiated-link path
(BRCMF_STA_DWDS actually going set on a real association) is untested
here and should be called exactly that: firmware-confirmed-accepting,
driver-wired, functionally unverified pending a real DWDS-capable peer.

Compile-tested against openwrt-sdk-25.12.5-bcm53xx-generic, backports-
6.18.26, this router's exact shipping kernel/driver combination.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c	2026-07-26 10:45:17.394226652 -0700
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c	2026-07-26 10:45:17.394226652 -0700
@@ -3181,6 +3181,25 @@
 		sinfo->sta_flags.set |= BIT(NL80211_STA_FLAG_TDLS_PEER);
 	else
 		sinfo->sta_flags.set &= ~BIT(NL80211_STA_FLAG_TDLS_PEER);
+	/*
+	 * Dynamic WDS (DWDS): firmware negotiates 4-address framing
+	 * per-station with another DWDS-capable Broadcom AP/repeater, which
+	 * lets that link carry real client MAC addresses end-to-end instead
+	 * of NAT/proxy-ARP hiding them behind this device's own MAC. The
+	 * firmware already reports these bits per station (BRCMF_STA_DWDS_CAP
+	 * = peer negotiated DWDS support, BRCMF_STA_DWDS = link is actively
+	 * using it) - the driver has carried the #defines since day one but
+	 * never read them. There is no existing generic nl80211 station-info
+	 * field for this (checked: no NL80211_STA_FLAG_4ADDR_MODE or
+	 * equivalent exists), so this is intentionally log-only for now
+	 * rather than force-fitting it onto an unrelated flag - a real nl80211
+	 * attribute for this is an upstream API discussion, not something to
+	 * invent unilaterally here.
+	 */
+	if (sta_flags & (BRCMF_STA_DWDS_CAP | BRCMF_STA_DWDS))
+		brcmf_dbg(CONN, "%pM: dwds_cap=%d dwds_active=%d\n", mac,
+			  !!(sta_flags & BRCMF_STA_DWDS_CAP),
+			  !!(sta_flags & BRCMF_STA_DWDS));
 	if (sta_flags & BRCMF_STA_ASSOC) {
 		sinfo->filled |= BIT_ULL(NL80211_STA_INFO_CONNECTED_TIME);
 		sinfo->connected_time = le32_to_cpu(sta_info_le.in);
@@ -5318,6 +5337,28 @@
 			goto exit;
 		}
 
+		/*
+		 * Advertise DWDS (Dynamic WDS) capability on this AP bsscfg.
+		 * Confirmed live on this exact firmware/chip (BCM43602,
+		 * netgear,r8000): the "dwds" iovar is accepted and durably
+		 * retained (err=0, verified via readback) where the classic
+		 * "wds" iovar is rejected outright (err=-52) - see
+		 * hwoffload-research/psta-probe/dwds_probe.c. This only
+		 * advertises the capability; it does not force anything on
+		 * ordinary (non-DWDS) clients, which never set
+		 * BRCMF_STA_DWDS_CAP and are completely unaffected - matching
+		 * how wpa_auth/wsec/mfp are set unconditionally just above.
+		 * A real DWDS *link* still needs a peer that also speaks
+		 * Broadcom's DWDS negotiation (another Broadcom-family AP or
+		 * repeater in wl/dhd-compatible mesh/backhaul mode) - it is
+		 * not something an ordinary 802.11 client (a phone, an IoT
+		 * camera) can or will ever negotiate, regardless of this
+		 * change. Non-fatal if firmware rejects it on some other
+		 * chip/branch - AP bring-up must not depend on it.
+		 */
+		if (brcmf_fil_bsscfg_int_set(ifp, "dwds", 1))
+			brcmf_dbg(INFO, "dwds capability not accepted on this bsscfg\n");
+
 		brcmf_dbg(TRACE, "AP mode configuration complete\n");
 	} else if (dev_role == NL80211_IFTYPE_P2P_GO) {
 		err = brcmf_fil_iovar_int_set(ifp, "chanspec", chanspec);
